### Entra ID (Microsoft Identity Platform) — OAuth2 Authorization Code flow
### for the SAP MCP Gateway on Integration Suite.
###
### Run with the VS Code REST Client extension.
### Replace the client secret and the authorization code with your own values.
### Do NOT commit real secrets or codes — they are single-use / sensitive.

@tenant = ee9157fe-19b9-4e21-85da-f093ed5df295
@clientId = 74612d5d-0ebb-4105-9ba4-4d33a0e73ce9
@clientSecret = <your client secret>
@redirectUri = http://localhost:8080/callback
@scope = api://74612d5d-0ebb-4105-9ba4-4d33a0e73ce9/sap.access offline_access

### 1. Get the authorization code (open this URL in a browser)
# Sign in, consent, and copy the ?code= value from the localhost callback URL.
# GET (paste into a browser — this is not sent by REST Client):
#
# https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenant}}/oauth2/v2.0/authorize
#   ?client_id={{clientId}}
#   &response_type=code
#   &redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}
#   &scope=api://74612d5d-0ebb-4105-9ba4-4d33a0e73ce9/sap.access%20offline_access
#   &response_mode=query

### 2. Exchange the authorization code for an access_token
# Paste the fresh code from the ?code= callback (single-use, ~10 min).
# @name token
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenant}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&client_id={{clientId}}
&client_secret={{clientSecret}}
&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}
&scope={{scope}}
&code=<paste the fresh ?code= value here>

### 3. (Optional) Refresh the access_token using offline_access
# @name refresh
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenant}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token
&client_id={{clientId}}
&client_secret={{clientSecret}}
&scope={{scope}}
&refresh_token={{token.response.body.refresh_token}}

### 4. Initialize the MCP session (using the Entra ID bearer token)
@MCP-BTP-Server-URL = <your MCP Server URL>
# @name init
POST {{MCP-BTP-Server-URL}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "vscode-rest", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

### 5. List the exposed MCP tools
# @name toolsList
POST {{MCP-BTP-Server-URL}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Mcp-Session-Id: {{init.response.headers.mcp-session-id}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list"
}
